# homma-core backlog

Designed and deferred. Names are unbackticked on purpose so the design-doc lint
does not look for them in source.

## The daemon re-running the slow half

The hook runs what a push can wait for. Full feature matrices, coverage and the
publish dry run are the slow half, and the daemon, which is homma's one
background actor, could run them on a new dev tip and append a second record
that the release then prefers. Named so it lands on the daemon rather than on a
second scheduler.

## Per-lint statuses from mockspace

The commit status mechanism generalises: every mockspace lint can post its own
status on the sha it judged, and a ruleset can require any subset of them on
either trunk. That is mockspace's to build and homma's to consume, and the
context name a lint posts under wants deciding once, together.
